<title>UK: LIFFE dismisses rumours of security alert.</title>
<headline>LIFFE dismisses rumours of security alert.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange (LIFFE) dismissed rumours that its Dowgate Hill building had been closed because of a bomb alert.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm still sitting here and the alarm buzzers aren't ringing. Nothing is going on here,&quot; said a LIFFE spokesman contacted by Reuters about the rumours.</p>
</text>
